## Code & Content Standards

### Tech Stack
- SvelteKit (migrating from older Svelte/Vite setup)
- Tailwind CSS for styling
- Vercel for hosting
- TypeScript preferred, JavaScript acceptable

### SEO Requirements (Every Page)
- Schema markup: LocalBusiness, RealEstateAgent, FAQPage as appropriate
- Meta titles < 60 chars, descriptions < 155 chars
- Open Graph + Twitter Card meta tags
- Canonical URLs on all pages
- Mobile-first responsive design
- Core Web Vitals: LCP < 2.5s, FID < 100ms, CLS < 0.1
- E-E-A-T signals: author bio, credentials, local expertise proof

### Content Voice
- Write as Dr. Jan Duffy — authoritative, warm, direct.
- Prioritize neighborhood-specific detail over generic national advice.
- Anchor comparisons to lifestyle (golf, 55+, commute, schools, HOA,
  views) and price band.
- Explain jargon in plain language for consumers.
- All content should be repurposable for email, video scripts, or
  listing presentations.

### File & Component Conventions
- Component naming: PascalCase
- File naming: kebab-case
- Never commit .env files or API keys
- Conventional commits: feat:, fix:, chore:, docs:

## Integration Points
- RealScout: Property search widgets (embedded via script tags)
- Follow Up Boss: CRM / lead capture
- Homebot.ai: Client retention
- CallAction: Phone / lead routing
- BombBomb: Video email
- CloudCMA: Comparative market analysis
